<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  THE NEGOTIATING ARC of the connect object (handoff §4, «Подключаемся — одна дуга по
  кругу, 1100 мс»), ported from the prototype's own SVG:

      <svg viewBox="0 0 214 214" style="animation:spin 1100ms linear infinite">
        <circle cx="107" cy="107" r="85" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-dasharray="104 430" />

  The viewport is 214, i.e. @dimen/connect_object, so one viewport unit is one dp and
  the arc rides the ACTIVE ring without this file having to know where the ring is.

  RADIUS 84 AND NOT THE PROTOTYPE'S 85, and this is the owner's «он не ровно по линии
  вокруг кнопки крутится, а чуть выше».

  The prototype draws the ring it rides as a CSS border — `inset:22px; border:2px solid`
  — and a CSS border is drawn INSIDE the box, so its centre line is at 85 - 1 = 84. Its
  arc is an SVG stroke at r=85, which is centred ON the path. The two disagree by half a
  stroke, and at 214 CSS pixels on a desktop that is invisible; at 3x on a phone it is
  3px of a 6px line, i.e. the arc plainly riding outside its own track.

  The port inherits the same geometry from the other side: HomeFragment.buildConnectObject
  strokes the inner ring with a GradientDrawable, which insets the oval by half the stroke
  exactly as CSS does, so the ring's centre line is 84 here too. So the arc is 84. Nothing
  else moves — inset 22 in a 214 box and a 2dp stroke are still §4's numbers, and this is
  what they arithmetically mean.

  trimPathEnd is the dash: the circumference at r=84 is 527.79, the prototype shows 104
  of it, and 104/527.79 = 0.197. ONE arc and never a train of segments (§11 grabl 7).

  It is WHITE and tinted at the ImageView (`app:tint="?attr/colorAccentFigure"`), the
  same way @drawable/ic_flow_arc is tinted on the прогрузка ring — a vector cannot carry
  a theme attribute in strokeColor without forking this file per theme.

  IT IS THE BRIGHT HALF OF A PAIR. The prototype's negotiating ring is the accent at 30 %
  (`rgba(76,141,255,.30)`) with the arc at full strength on top of it; the port used to
  paint both at full and they cancelled out — «надо цвет чутка темнее сделать чтобы был
  акцент и видно, что идёт анимация». The contrast is restored on the RING's side, where
  the design puts it: see HomeFragment.dimRingTrack.

  The revolution is NOT here: it is one infinite ObjectAnimator on ROTATION at
  @integer/motion_spin, linear, started and stopped by HomeFragment. That is the route
  FlowOverlay.startArc already takes, and it is what finally lands §4's 1100 exactly —
  a Material CircularProgressIndicator owns its own clock and cannot be told this number.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="@dimen/connect_object"
    android:height="@dimen/connect_object"
    android:viewportWidth="214"
    android:viewportHeight="214">
    <path
        android:pathData="M107,23 A84,84 0 0,1 107,191 A84,84 0 0,1 107,23"
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeWidth="2"
        android:trimPathEnd="0.197"
        android:trimPathStart="0" />
</vector>
